<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Task #48 (デフォルトメールアプリ対応): identical to Otegami-iOS.entitlements
	plus the one extra `com.apple.developer.mail-client` key — see
	docs/default-mail-app.md for the full story. A *separate* file (rather
	than always including this key in Otegami-iOS.entitlements) because
	Apple must specifically grant this capability per-app before it can be
	requested at all: a profile built against a capability the App ID
	doesn't have registered fails to sign, so committing it unconditionally
	would break every build until the request is approved. project.yml
	switches which of these two files `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=iphoneos*]`/
	`[sdk=iphonesimulator*]` actually uses via the `OTEGAMI_MAIL_CLIENT_ENTITLEMENT`
	xcconfig flag (Config/Shared.xcconfig's doc comment) — default `NO`
	(this file unused, current behavior unchanged), flip to `YES` in
	Config/Local.xcconfig once Apple's grant lands and the capability is
	enabled for this App ID in the Developer portal.

	Keep this file's other keys in sync with Otegami-iOS.entitlements by
	hand — see that file's doc comment for what each one does and why.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(OTEGAMI_APP_GROUP)</string>
	</array>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(OTEGAMI_KEYCHAIN_GROUP)</string>
	</array>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-kvstore-identifier</key>
	<string>$(TeamIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)</string>
	<!--
	Communication Notifications — see Otegami-iOS.entitlements' doc comment
	for what this enables and why it stays out of Otegami-macOS.entitlements.
	Kept in sync with that file by hand, like every other shared key here.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.communication</key>
	<true/>
	<!--
	The capability this whole file exists for — lets this app become a
	user-selectable default for `mailto:` links / the Mail role once Apple
	has granted the request (Info.plist's OtegamiMailClientEntitlementEnabled
	key, which `DefaultMailAppSettingsView` reads, mirrors this same
	`OTEGAMI_MAIL_CLIENT_ENTITLEMENT` flag so the in-app UI and the actual
	signed capability can never disagree about whether this build has it).
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.mail-client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
